"Choosing season is adolescence in the Rapports, when a child picks between knight and wizard."
"It begins at one's first ceremony where some knights request rest, and ends when one announces."
"Instructors must teach as if any future were possible; others wait to advise or celebrate."
"Almost everyone from the Rapport children's school becomes a knight or a wizard sworn to aid them."
"Historically, cycles forcibly expanded the knight population until the cost outweighed rewards."
"Older knights who swore in the worse cycles revived the good traditions."
"A choosing season can be delayed, for example a year to mourn."
